  "description": "The 2026 election for New York's 9th Congressional District will determine who represents central and southern Brooklyn, including neighborhoods such as Flatbush, Crown Heights, and East New York, in the U.S. House of Representatives. Incumbent Democrat Yvette Clarke, first elected in 2006 and serving the 9th District since 2013, faces a competitive Democratic primary challenge from Michael Goldfarb, a financial technology executive and Blackstone alum, and Joshua Bristol, a Brooklyn organizer and democratic socialist. The Republican nominee is Joel Anabilah-Azumah, a small business owner and college volleyball coach. The district is heavily Democratic, with a Cook Partisan Voting Index of D+22, making the Democratic primary the decisive contest.",
